    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="0460" n="378" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg378"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/879.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of War to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >War Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic">December 20,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your letter of December 16,
                        1910,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d496-f1"/> communicating to this Department the
                    suggestion of the Mexican ambassador that a force be sent to Presidio, Tex., to
                    arrest and disarm revolutionists who might cross the frontier at that place, I
                    have the honor to inclose for your information a copy of a telegram of December
                    18, 1910, on the subject to the commanding general, department of Texas, and a
                    copy of his response thereto.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Shaw
                    Oliver.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d496-a1.xml" xpointer="d496-a1"/>
